Short:        Native AirPrint/IPP for AmigaOS
Uploader:     Andreas "Andiweli" Stuermer
Author:       Andreas "Andiweli" Stuermer
Type:         driver/print
Version:      1.2
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

AmiAirPrint is a native AirPrint/IPP printer solution for classic AmigaOS.
It integrates with printer.device and prints directly to compatible network
printers without CUPS or a PC print server.

Main features:

- AmigaOS 3.0+ and Motorola 68000 compatible
- PWG Raster graphics printing through printer.device
- PDF and PostScript output when advertised by the printer
- processed PRT:/CMD_WRITE text printing with Latin-1 support
- color and monochrome output
- Portrait and Landscape
- duplex long-edge and short-edge printing
- printer-reported paper source / tray selection
- printer capability-based DPI selection
- paper/media, quality and color-mode selection
- 10-100% graphics scaling and optional centering
- GadTools preferences program for AmigaOS 3.0/3.1
- ReAction preferences program for AmigaOS 3.2+
- Advanced print options in both preferences programs
- locale.library support with built-in English fallback
- maintained German translation source
- local printer discovery through mDNS/DNS-SD and SSDP
- IPP capability query and capability-aware test page
- HTTP/IPP compatibility handling for problematic printer firmware
- Installer 43.3 compatible installation script

Release 1.2 also fixes FinalWriter striped-printing / endless blank-page
behaviour and Wordworth multi-page graphics/form-feed handling.

Verified application paths include PersonalPaint, MultiView, FinalWriter,
Wordworth 5 and IBrowse processed text, including multi-page duplex output.

Component versions:

- package / preferences: 1.2
- AirPrint printer driver: 43.43
- airprint.device: 1.2
- diagnostic tools: 1.2

Requirements:

- TCP/IP stack providing bsdsocket.library
- IPv4-reachable IPP/AirPrint printer

AmiAirPrint currently uses plain HTTP/IPP. TLS-only IPPS endpoints are not
supported.

After installation, select AirPrint as the printer driver and Parallel as the
port in the normal AmigaOS Printer preferences. Parallel is only a classic
printer.device compatibility selection; network data is sent directly through
airprint.device.

AmiAirPrint is released under the MIT License.
The embedded font8x8 Latin-1 bitmap data is Public Domain.
